appears on the deriving type.}
\label{tab:ch18-api}
\small
\begin{tabular}{@{}L{0.30\textwidth}L{0.62\textwidth}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Entity} & \textbf{Description} \\
\midrule
\code{lit<Suffix>(f)} & Factory for one registered suffix. \code{Suffix} is a \code{FixedString}, so the suffix text is a compile-time constant; \code{f} is the handler, called as \code{f(long double)}. \\
\code{literal_set(e...)} & Factory for a set. The entries are stored in a \code{std::tuple}, so the set's size and the types of its handlers are fixed at compile time. \\
